ONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n* Reproducible in v4.5.1.stable.mono\n* Older versions not tested\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot v4.5.1.stable.mono - Compatibility\n\n### Issue description\n\nI tried to create an async extension of HttpRequest but it simply does not show up in the global class hierarchy:\n```csharp\n[GlobalClass]\npublic partial class AsyncHttpRequest : HttpRequest\n{\n    [Export] public string BaseAddressLink { get; set; } = \"\";\n\n    [Signal] public delegate void RequestFinishedEventHandler();\n\n    private bool _isRequesting;\n    \n    public async Task<HttpResult> RequestAsync(string endpoint,\n        string[] customHeaders = null,\n        HttpClient.Method method = HttpClient.Method.Get,\n        string requestData = \"\")\n    {\n        if (_isRequesting)\n            return HttpResult.FromError(Error.Busy);\n\n        _isRequesting = true;\n        try\n        {\n            var error = Request($\"{BaseAddressLink}/{endpoint}\", customHeaders, method, requestData);\n            if (error != Error.Ok) return HttpResult.FromError(error);\n\n            var args = await ToSignal(this, HttpRequest.SignalName.RequestCompleted);\n            EmitSignalRequestFinished();\n            return HttpResult.FromSynchronousRequest(args);\n        }\n        finally\n        {\n            _isRequesting = false;\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new script\n- Extend HttpRequest\n- Annotate as GlobalClass\n- Build\n- Check \"add new node\" menu\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nI do not think it is necessary for this. It is a small bug that is probably well known (and maybe even an intenional feature).","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"M